if GameState.get_flag("act1/talked_to_elder") == true:
	Elder Mishka has not moved from her bench. She is watching the north road, where the mist has thickened into a low white wall. "Go on, child. But keep your eyes on the water."
	jump end
Elder Mishka looks up from her bench and her whole face creases into a smile. "There he is. The boy who used to steal my honey cakes, grown tall enough to carry a sword."
She takes your hand in both of hers, and her smile fades by a degree. "A thick mist is rolling in off the water. Strong and low, the kind that swallows a man's own feet. It came up too fast to be weather."
- "It is only the season, grandmother."
	She pats your hand, kindly, and does not agree with you.
- "You sound afraid."
	"I have lived long enough to know the difference between afraid and certain."
"Something feels off today. The birds went quiet before dawn and they have not started again. I can sense a darkness approaching, and it is not coming from the sky."
She lets go of your hand and folds her own in her lap. "Go and say your goodbyes properly. Do not let an old woman be the last voice you hear today."
[signal arg="set_flag act1/talked_to_elder"]
label end
